# Brand assets — Taskcover Agency

## Official assets

Drop the official Taskcover logo package here. The files below are expected by
the site (`src/lib/site.ts`):

| Expected file               | Purpose                                  |
| --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| `taskcover-horizontal.svg`  | Header / footer wordmark                 |
| `taskcover-icon.svg`        | Favicon, social avatar, small UI badges  |
| `og-default.svg`            | Default Open Graph / Twitter share image |

These paths are currently filled with **on-brand placeholder SVGs** using the
official Taskcover gradient (green → emerald → teal → blue). Replace each file
with the official asset when provided.

## Logo usage rules

See [`docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`](../../docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md) for the full guide.

- Prefer transparent / white-background variants. **Do not** use the
  black-background logo variant in the main UI.
- Do not distort, recolor, stretch, or crop the logo.
- Use the horizontal logo in the header.
- Use the icon/avatar version for favicon, small badges, social preview, and
  compact UI.

## Replacing placeholders

1. Replace each file in this folder with the official asset (same filename).
2. If official assets use different filenames, update `src/lib/site.ts`
   (`siteConfig.logo` and `siteConfig.ogImage`).